  "text": "None of the three formulas is correct, though I'm working from recall rather than a verified source.\n\nThe check I can make without a source is small cases. The automorphisms of $\\mathbb{Z}_{2^e}$ number $2^{e-1}$. I recall Conder's tables giving $\\mathrm{Skew}(8)=6$ and $\\mathrm{Skew}(16)=16$, though I haven't confirmed them here.\n\n- **Solution 1**, $2^{2e-3}+2^{e-2}$: at $e=3$ this gives $10$, not $6$.\n- **Solution 2**, $2^{e-2}(e+1)$: at $e=3$ this gives $8$, not $6$.\n- **Solution 3**, $2^e-2$: at $e=3$ this gives $6$, which matches, but at $e=4$ it gives $14$, not $16$. Its two-family construction also double-counts the automorphisms and does not establish that the $\\varphi_t$ are skew morphisms at all.\n\nThe recalled values $2, 6, 16, 40$ for $e=2,\\dots,5$ fit $e\\cdot 2^{e-2}$, which would mean the non-automorphism skew morphisms number $2^{e-2}(e-2)$. I have not verified this formula, so treat it as a hypothesis. Whatever the exact formula, the three proposed answers fail the $e=3$ or $e=4$ checks, so none is supported.\n\nCHOICE: NONE",
